SUMMARY:Observe the Moon Day - Night Event
DESCRIPTION:[vc_row][vc_column width=”1/1″][vc_column_text uncode_shortcode_id=”115847″]Mark your calendars for Saturday\, September 19\, to celebrate International Observe the Moon Day with the North Museum! \nIn the evening\, join us right here at the North Museum at 7:30 PM to observe the Moon with us! You can expect a view of the Moon through our telescopes\, and some fun Moon facts! Standard admission and planetarium fees apply for the activities during the day\, but the evening Moon observing will be free to the public. You can sign up for the observing night here.[/vc_column_text][vc_button button_color=”color-395923″ size=”btn-xl” radius=”btn-circle” outline=”yes” border_width=”0″ link=”url:https%3A%2F%2F68796.blackbaudhosting.com%2F68796%2FInternational-Observe-the-Moon-Night” el_class=”home-ads-btn” button_color_type=”uncode-palette” uncode_shortcode_id=”170647″]Sign-Up[/vc_button][/vc_column][/vc_row]
URL:https://northmuseum.org/events/observe-the-moon-day-night-event/
LOCATION:North Museum\, PA\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://northmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/moonday-cal-night.jpg
END:VEVENT
